      "title": "Executive Brief",
      "content": "**Bottom line.** **Hand-Foot-Mouth Disease** is a **low-priority, not rising surveillance signal**. It warrants active review, but the present evidence does not by itself establish an emergency. Across 2025-05-23 to 2026-05-22, the dataset records 29,359 cases and 0 deaths across 1 disease; the latest observation contributes 800 cases.\n\n**Why it matters.** The practical question is whether the recent increase is becoming persistent or whether it reflects seasonality, reporting catch-up, or ascertainment changes. Because rate denominators are unavailable, this report should be read as a burden-and-trend assessment rather than a population-risk estimate. Numeric confidence is 90%, with the main uncertainty sitting in source definitions and lag.\n\n### Near-Term Watch\n- Confirm whether the next reporting periods remain above the recent background level.\n- Check whether increases are concentrated by place, age group, or reporting source once stratified data are available.\n- Treat corroborating event-based reports as signal-strengthening evidence; treat a return toward background as support for a timing or seasonal explanation.",
